<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Crusader states</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Crusader state, Crusaders, Crusader</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Crusader states were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> Christian states established in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a>, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a>, the County of Edessa, the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> and the County of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripoli">Tripoli</a>. They fought against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>, which recaptured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> in 1187. The last of their strongholds was taken by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a> with the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a> in 1291.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/crusader-states.jpg" alt="Crusader states" width="320" height="309" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean Colombe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CouncilofClermont.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
